**So what?** The pin was the occasion; the error-bar result is the discovery. The site has been treating "marginalized" as a synonym for "the correlations are handled". The tables say the galaxy-level width stays three to seven times the pooled-point width after marginalization, because the disagreement between galaxies about the transition shape is a curve-level property that neither per-galaxy slides nor per-point scatter can express.
